preferred-citation:
  type: manuscript
  title: >-
    Identifiability and Predictability Are Distinct: Measured Preimages
    Across Generative Systems
  abstract: >-
    For a hypothesis space H of candidate generators and an observation O, we
    measure the preimage P(O) exactly rather than searching for a minimal
    generator. Unresolved information decomposes into observation deficiency
    and degeneracy of H; the first term is removable only where the observer
    may intervene; and the per-generator coordinates i_O(g) and p_k(g) do not
    determine one another. A pre-registered enumeration of 1,500,625
    partially observed Markov chains meets all five frozen criteria, and
    changing only the admissible intervention class moves 82.0% of generators
    between threshold-defined regimes.
  authors:
    - family-names: Ward
      given-names: Gregory J.
      email: greg@smartledger.technology
    - family-names: Daugherty
      given-names: Bryan W.
    - family-names: Ryan
